<!--Post: 3786--><!--Time: 1105231634-->
<!--p:--><tr bgcolor="#f7f7f7"><td valign=top width=200><a name="POST3786"><font face="Verdana" size="1"><b><!--email--><!--/email--><!--name-->Affie4u<!--/name--></b></a><br>Username: <!--field:uname-->Affie4u<!--/field--><br><br>Registered: <!--field:registered-->12-2004<!--/field--><br><!--field:ip_address--><!--/field--></font></font></td><td valign=top><font face="Verdana" size="1"><table width=100% border=0 cellspacing=0 cellpadding=0><tr><td align=left><font face="Verdana" size="1">Posted on Saturday, January 08, 2005 - 4:47 pm: &nbsp;&nbsp;</font></td><td align=right></td></tr></table><hr noshade size=0><!--Text-->Do you think BTK works at a library? Since he left a note in a book at the library &amp; writes on computers/typwriter? <BR> <BR>Or maybe he was a proffessor at the college? That is how he new PJ and since he is writing his own book, a lot of proffessors do that.<!--/Text--></td></tr>
<!--/Post: 3786-->
<!--Post: 3862--><!--Time: 1105342970-->
<!--p:--><tr bgcolor="#cccccc"><td valign=top width=200><a name="POST3862"><font face="Verdana" size="1"><b><!--email--><!--/email--><!--name-->Ivy_leaguer<!--/name--></b></a><br>Username: <!--field:uname-->Ivy_leaguer<!--/field--><br><br>Registered: <!--field:registered-->10-2004<!--/field--><br><!--field:ip_address--><!--/field--></font></font></td><td valign=top><font face="Verdana" size="1"><table width=100% border=0 cellspacing=0 cellpadding=0><tr><td align=left><font face="Verdana" size="1">Posted on Sunday, January 09, 2005 - 11:42 pm: &nbsp;&nbsp;</font></td><td align=right></td></tr></table><hr noshade size=0><!--Text-->The BTK Strangler considers his relationship with Wichita State University important. It seems likely the unknown subject was either an undergraduate or postgraduate student at Wichita State University. Student life would provide him with anonymity. This gave him the confidence to refer to Wichita State University in his correspondences with the police and media. A member of the teaching faculty is also a possiblity. If, he taught at Wichita State University it seems more likely the unknown subject was a tutor, rather than a professor or head of faculty. Junior academics tend to be unknown and obscure.  <BR> <BR>It seems less likely the BTK Strangler was an employee of the library at Wichita State University. The number of library employees at Wichita State would be a small number compared to the number of students and teaching faculty. It would be simpler to determine the identity of library staff.  <BR> <BR>The BTK Strangler&#39;s references to Wichita State University is an attempt to convince the police and public he is intelligent. It seems he wants them to know he is college educated and considerably more intelligent than the police and the public. It seems the unknown subject considers intelligence an important quality. He uses it to taunt, manipulate and control the police and public.<!--/Text--></td></tr>
<!--/Post: 3862-->
<!--Post: 3876--><!--Time: 1105374824-->
<!--p:--><tr bgcolor="#f7f7f7"><td valign=top width=200><a name="POST3876"><font face="Verdana" size="1"><b><!--email--><!--/email--><!--name-->Jujuree<!--/name--></b></a><br>Username: <!--field:uname-->Jujuree<!--/field--><br><br>Registered: <!--field:registered-->12-2004<!--/field--><br><!--field:ip_address--><!--/field--></font></font></td><td valign=top><font face="Verdana" size="1"><table width=100% border=0 cellspacing=0 cellpadding=0><tr><td align=left><font face="Verdana" size="1">Posted on Monday, January 10, 2005 - 8:33 am: &nbsp;&nbsp;</font></td><td align=right></td></tr></table><hr noshade size=0><!--Text-->I go back and forth on this.  I think it&#39;s very possible that he is/was on the faculty at WSU.  However, as Ivy Leaguer pointed out, BTK has made such a point of stressing a relationship with the college I have to wonder if he&#39;s overcompensating, trying to create an illusion that he is far more educated than he really is. <BR> <BR>Maybe he is a college dropout? <!--/Text--></td></tr>
<!--/Post: 3876-->
<!--Post: 3886--><!--Time: 1105393188-->
<!--p:--><tr bgcolor="#cccccc"><td valign=top width=200><a name="POST3886"><font face="Verdana" size="1"><b><!--email--><!--/email--><!--name-->Juno<!--/name--></b></a><br>Username: <!--field:uname-->Juno<!--/field--><br><br>Registered: <!--field:registered-->5-2004<!--/field--><br><!--field:ip_address--><!--/field--></font></font></td><td valign=top><font face="Verdana" size="1"><table width=100% border=0 cellspacing=0 cellpadding=0><tr><td align=left><font face="Verdana" size="1">Posted on Monday, January 10, 2005 - 1:39 pm: &nbsp;&nbsp;</font></td><td align=right></td></tr></table><hr noshade size=0><!--Text-->I feel quite confident there is a library connection, though i am wavering on whether it is public or academic.  I am leaning toward public, for the following reasons: <BR> <BR>A library employee would have access to people&#39;s library accounts, which includes their library card number along with other personal information such as addresses and telephone numbers. <BR> <BR>The victims would have all been more likely &#40;i am making an assumption here&#41; to have all been public library patrons rather than all having been university library patrons.  I could be wrong about that if Shirley Vian or either of the Oteros used the university library. <BR> <BR>I am assuming that BTK read a lot about other serial killers and other related subjects.  At the time his primary source of information would have been a library. A library employee would have been able to interlibrary loan materials without having them be connected to him personally.  For example, he could have created &#34;dummy&#34; library accounts for his use, or ordered them under someone else&#39;s account and then read and returned them.  Again, this was before automated notification systems and could easily have been accomplished. <BR> <BR>If this person did not work in a library, i think he was either related to someone who worked in a library or had a level of access &#40;due to type of employment,university for example&#41; that the general pubic does not have. <BR>  <!--/Text--></td></tr>
<!--/Post: 3886-->
<!--Post: 3887--><!--Time: 1105393826-->
<!--p:--><tr bgcolor="#f7f7f7"><td valign=top width=200><a name="POST3887"><font face="Verdana" size="1"><b><!--email--><!--/email--><!--name-->Juno<!--/name--></b></a><br>Username: <!--field:uname-->Juno<!--/field--><br><br>Registered: <!--field:registered-->5-2004<!--/field--><br><!--field:ip_address--><!--/field--></font></font></td><td valign=top><font face="Verdana" size="1"><table width=100% border=0 cellspacing=0 cellpadding=0><tr><td align=left><font face="Verdana" size="1">Posted on Monday, January 10, 2005 - 1:50 pm: &nbsp;&nbsp;</font></td><td align=right></td></tr></table><hr noshade size=0><!--Text-->I regard to the above, it occurred to me that he may have just read a lot of detective magazines, but I still think there is a library connection<!--/Text--></td></tr>
<!--/Post: 3887-->
<!--Post: 3919--><!--Time: 1105416287-->
<!--p:--><tr bgcolor="#cccccc"><td valign=top width=200><a name="POST3919"><font face="Verdana" size="1"><b><!--email--><!--/email--><!--name-->George<!--/name--></b></a><br>Username: <!--field:uname-->George<!--/field--><br><br>Registered: <!--field:registered-->7-2004<!--/field--><br><!--field:ip_address--><!--/field--></font></font></td><td valign=top><font face="Verdana" size="1"><table width=100% border=0 cellspacing=0 cellpadding=0><tr><td align=left><font face="Verdana" size="1">Posted on Monday, January 10, 2005 - 8:04 pm: &nbsp;&nbsp;</font></td><td align=right></td></tr></table><hr noshade size=0><!--Text-->I wonder if it&#39;s possible to determine the reading requirements of any Criminology or Law Enforcement course WSU offered at the time. Even if not, <i>some</i> sort of library connection is credible, I agree. A college dropout also makes some sense; referencing WSU may indicate a teacher or student, I agree, but it may also indicate a dropout whose ego demands recognition as an educated person. Perhaps BTK came from a family which <i>expected</i> a college degree -- I came from such a family and disappointed them -- and BTK felt extra pressure to present himself as educated?  <BR> <BR>The definite BTK crimes, of course, occurred on a Tuesday, Thursday, Thursday, Thursday and Tuesday, over a period of twelve and one-half years. This aids a teacher theory and lessens a student theory, unless BTK was a sporadic &#40;or habitual&#41; student. I&#39;d point out the possibility that the Tuesday and Thursday days of the week may also be completely coincidental.  <BR> <BR><i>Or</i>, the 1974 Otero and Bright attacks, Tuesday and Thursday respectively, were noticed by BTK during <i>his nearly three-year hiatus</i> as appearing suspiciously &#34;college-related,&#34; and they <i>weren&#39;t</i> college-related but BTK wanted his next attacks, Thursday, Thursday, Tuesday to retain a &#34;college-related&#34; appearance to confuse his captors. This final scenario is unlikely as it assumes an awful lot of things, but I thought I&#39;d mention it. At any rate, I agree with Juno that a library of some sort plays a significant role in all of this. <BR><!--/Text--></td></tr>
<!--/Post: 3919-->
<!--Post: 3946--><!--Time: 1105443449-->
<!--p:--><tr bgcolor="#f7f7f7"><td valign=top width=200><a name="POST3946"><font face="Verdana" size="1"><b><!--email--><!--/email--><!--name-->Nugzter<!--/name--></b></a><br>Username: <!--field:uname-->Nugzter<!--/field--><br><br>Registered: <!--field:registered-->12-2004<!--/field--><br><!--field:ip_address--><!--/field--></font></font></td><td valign=top><font face="Verdana" size="1"><table width=100% border=0 cellspacing=0 cellpadding=0><tr><td align=left><font face="Verdana" size="1">Posted on Tuesday, January 11, 2005 - 3:37 am: &nbsp;&nbsp;</font></td><td align=right></td></tr></table><hr noshade size=0><!--Text-->Possible Library connections: <BR>Basics: Librarian, custodian, repaiman&#40;copier ect&#41;, teacher, student, admin, nerd. <BR>The library is his form of post office. So lets look at the things from outside the box. <BR>In the 70&#39;s and 80&#39;s the libray was a happening spot. Frequented more that today. Could be he would practice stalking women in the library. Come on guys, we all have done it. You see a hot girl in the science fiction section, so you manuver yourself to a spot where you can see better. Get a little closer. Victims have a connection to the library?  <BR>He can go there and fit in like a finger in a glove. Oh did I mention, wouldnt someone with gloves on stand out in the library? No prints on the letters. Had to have had gloves on. And you all know how libraians are, they got the whole library under the eagle eye. So he had to have been a regular. Who wore gloves. If he was uneducated he would not be smart enough to try to mislead the WPD to look at the library as a connection. Hes gone modern on us. No need for analog reading material. Its all done over the net now days.<!--/Text--></td></tr>
<!--/Post: 3946-->
<!--Post: 3949--><!--Time: 1105445912-->
<!--p:--><tr bgcolor="#cccccc"><td valign=top width=200><a name="POST3949"><font face="Verdana" size="1"><b><!--email--><!--/email--><!--name-->George<!--/name--></b></a><br>Username: <!--field:uname-->George<!--/field--><br><br>Registered: <!--field:registered-->7-2004<!--/field--><br><!--field:ip_address--><!--/field--></font></font></td><td valign=top><font face="Verdana" size="1"><table width=100% border=0 cellspacing=0 cellpadding=0><tr><td align=left><font face="Verdana" size="1">Posted on Tuesday, January 11, 2005 - 4:18 am: &nbsp;&nbsp;</font></td><td align=right></td></tr></table><hr noshade size=0><!--Text--><i>If he was uneducated he would not be smart enough to try to mislead the WPD to look at the library as a connection.</i>  <BR>Peter or Jake or one of their clones, many uneducated people are brilliant. Knowledge and intelligence are two different things. One doesn&#39;t need gloves if one has no criminal record and hence no prints on file. <BR> <!--/Text--></td></tr>
<!--/Post: 3949-->
<!--Post: 3959--><!--Time: 1105452100-->
<!--p:--><tr bgcolor="#f7f7f7"><td valign=top width=200><a name="POST3959"><font face="Verdana" size="1"><b><!--email--><!--/email--><!--name-->Nugzter<!--/name--></b></a><br>Username: <!--field:uname-->Nugzter<!--/field--><br><br>Registered: <!--field:registered-->12-2004<!--/field--><br><!--field:ip_address--><!--/field--></font></font></td><td valign=top><font face="Verdana" size="1"><table width=100% border=0 cellspacing=0 cellpadding=0><tr><td align=left><font face="Verdana" size="1">Posted on Tuesday, January 11, 2005 - 6:01 am: &nbsp;&nbsp;</font></td><td align=right></td></tr></table><hr noshade size=0><!--Text-->You ae missing the whole picture George. I have no criminal record, and if I was gonna off someone I&#39;d wear gloves. Just incase I&#39;m questioned and they want prints, they cant match me to the crime. Come on think about it. Knowledge is when you have leaned something and know extensily about the subject. Being a knowledgeable serial killer is not possible. He would be knowledgable of his cimes but not about serial killings. Unless he&#39;s a coppy cat &#40;and he sort of is&#41; But what I was refering to is that h must be educated. Think about it, Billy Bob dumb a&#42;&#42; send the cop to the library to look for a specific book by Dewwy decimal. He has to had &#34;knowledge&#34; of this library. He is not some loser guy who cant read. Come on George<!--/Text--></td></tr>
<!--/Post: 3959-->
<!--Post: 3963--><!--Time: 1105468675-->
<!--p:--><tr bgcolor="#cccccc"><td valign=top width=200><a name="POST3963"><font face="Verdana" size="1"><b><!--email--><!--/email--><!--name-->Juno<!--/name--></b></a><br>Username: <!--field:uname-->Juno<!--/field--><br><br>Registered: <!--field:registered-->5-2004<!--/field--><br><!--field:ip_address--><!--/field--></font></font></td><td valign=top><font face="Verdana" size="1"><table width=100% border=0 cellspacing=0 cellpadding=0><tr><td align=left><font face="Verdana" size="1">Posted on Tuesday, January 11, 2005 - 10:37 am: &nbsp;&nbsp;</font></td><td align=right></td></tr></table><hr noshade size=0><!--Text-->As far as Tuesday Thursdays.....some library systems&#39; branches have weird hours.  Like they are open 9-5 one day, 1-9 another day, 10-6 another day, closed on friday etc.  I am not familiar with the state of Wichita Public Libraries in the 70s and 80s or how large the system was and how many branches it had.   <BR> <BR>About the only thing I can agree with Nugzter with is that BTK may have been a &#34;regular&#34; at the library.  However, i think there is a closer connection than that.  Other than that, even though I am a &#34;NERD&#34; library employee, I can&#39;t say that I have &#34;practised stalking women at the library.&#34;  No, Nugzter...do not delude yourself....we have  not &#34;all done it.&#34;   <BR> <BR>At any rate, I think he felt very comfortable at the library and that is why the first letter was placed there.  An employee &#40;or volunteer&#41; could have done that with no fear of detection.<!--/Text--></td></tr>
<!--/Post: 3963-->
<!--Post: 3971--><!--Time: 1105480962-->
<!--p:--><tr bgcolor="#f7f7f7"><td valign=top width=200><a name="POST3971"><font face="Verdana" size="1"><b><!--email--><!--/email--><!--name-->Ivy_leaguer<!--/name--></b></a><br>Username: <!--field:uname-->Ivy_leaguer<!--/field--><br><br>Registered: <!--field:registered-->10-2004<!--/field--><br><!--field:ip_address--><!--/field--></font></font></td><td valign=top><font face="Verdana" size="1"><table width=100% border=0 cellspacing=0 cellpadding=0><tr><td align=left><font face="Verdana" size="1">Posted on Tuesday, January 11, 2005 - 2:02 pm: &nbsp;&nbsp;</font></td><td align=right></td></tr></table><hr noshade size=0><!--Text-->It seems college and libraries are important to the BTK Strangler. I suspect the unknown subject graduated from college with an undergraduate degree before 1974 and possibly completed a postgraduate degree during his three year sabbatical. He seems to enjoy libraries and is familiar with them. A few students prefer studying in the library rather than socializing and have a strong understanding of the catalog and library staff protocol. Some are employed part-time in their college library. <BR> <BR>It seems plausible the BTK Strangler attended college, but did not graduate. The references to Wichita State University and libraries may be an attempt to project the facade he could be educated. This scenario is likely, but not as likely as the unknown subject graduating from college and spending most of his time in the  college or public library studying and possibly employed there to pay for tuition.     <!--/Text--></td></tr>
<!--/Post: 3971-->
<!--Post: 3972--><!--Time: 1105485447-->
<!--p:--><tr bgcolor="#cccccc"><td valign=top width=200><a name="POST3972"><font face="Verdana" size="1"><b><!--email--><!--/email--><!--name-->Steve_huff<!--/name--></b></a><br>Username: <!--field:uname-->Steve_huff<!--/field--><br><br>Registered: <!--field:registered-->12-2004<!--/field--><br><!--field:ip_address--><!--/field--></font></font></td><td valign=top><font face="Verdana" size="1"><table width=100% border=0 cellspacing=0 cellpadding=0><tr><td align=left><font face="Verdana" size="1">Posted on Tuesday, January 11, 2005 - 3:17 pm: &nbsp;&nbsp;</font></td><td align=right></td></tr></table><hr noshade size=0><!--Text-->&#34;It seems plausible the BTK Strangler attended college, but did not graduate. The references to Wichita State University and libraries may be an attempt to project the facade he could be educated. This scenario is likely, but not as likely as the unknown subject graduating from college and spending most of his time in the college or public library studying and possibly employed there to pay for tuition.&#34; <BR> <BR>Ivy, your cool reasoning and knowledge is always refreshing after reading some of the delusional ravings on other message boards. <i>&#40;and I mean many different boards, not just the one that probably leapt to mind...&#41;</i> <BR> <BR>I find the most plausible scenario to be the one where he did not graduate. I believe this is a man concerned about seeming literate, creative, intellectual, but he does not understand what truly demonstrates these qualities. Is not a hallmark of many sociopathic personalities an overriding concern with facade as opposed to substance? As long as they can <i>project</i> the image they want, they feel safe, as if they are compensating. Descriptions of such personalities often highlight their glibness, how they will seem on the surface to know a great deal about a wide variety of things.  <BR> <BR>That said, I would agree that he probably likes the library, for a multitude of reasons. I don&#39;t doubt he&#39;s a habitual reader, nor do I doubt that he may satisfy his &#34;loner&#34; side <i>&#40;because I think we&#39;re talking about an individual who has both a loner side but can project seeming sociability&#41;,</i> by sequestering himself in a library to study up on, say, other killers in privacy. <BR> <BR>One thing I see mentioned earlier in this thread is the possibility he was a library volunteer or employee...I have little other than gut to go on, but I don&#39;t see that. His library use is closer to to Ivy_leaguer&#39;s explanation: &#34;A few students prefer studying in the library rather than socializing...&#34;<!--/Text--></td></tr>
<!--/Post: 3972-->
<!--Post: 3974--><!--Time: 1105489078-->
<!--p:--><tr bgcolor="#f7f7f7"><td valign=top width=200><a name="POST3974"><font face="Verdana" size="1"><b><!--email--><!--/email--><!--name-->Ivy_leaguer<!--/name--></b></a><br>Username: <!--field:uname-->Ivy_leaguer<!--/field--><br><br>Registered: <!--field:registered-->10-2004<!--/field--><br><!--field:ip_address--><!--/field--></font></font></td><td valign=top><font face="Verdana" size="1"><table width=100% border=0 cellspacing=0 cellpadding=0><tr><td align=left><font face="Verdana" size="1">Posted on Tuesday, January 11, 2005 - 4:17 pm: &nbsp;&nbsp;</font></td><td align=right></td></tr></table><hr noshade size=0><!--Text-->Steve, <BR> <BR>I appreciate your kind comments. <BR> <BR>My assertion the BTK Strangler is a college graduate rather than a college drop out is based on several forensic psychologists, such as Michael Kelleher, Deborah Schurman-Kauflin and Pat Brown crafting profiles mentioning the unknown subject most probably possesses an undergraduate degree. Brown refers to a person of interest who is currently living in Wichita and who shares several characteristics with psychological portraits of the BTK Strangler. The person of interest attended Wichita State University and then studied accounting and business at a local business school. He believes he possesses superior intelligence.  <!--/Text--></td></tr>
<!--/Post: 3974-->
<!--Post: 3987--><!--Time: 1105501986-->
<!--p:--><tr bgcolor="#cccccc"><td valign=top width=200><a name="POST3987"><font face="Verdana" size="1"><b><!--email--><!--/email--><!--name-->George<!--/name--></b></a><br>Username: <!--field:uname-->George<!--/field--><br><br>Registered: <!--field:registered-->7-2004<!--/field--><br><!--field:ip_address--><!--/field--></font></font></td><td valign=top><font face="Verdana" size="1"><table width=100% border=0 cellspacing=0 cellpadding=0><tr><td align=left><font face="Verdana" size="1">Posted on Tuesday, January 11, 2005 - 7:53 pm: &nbsp;&nbsp;</font></td><td align=right></td></tr></table><hr noshade size=0><!--Text-->Nugzter, I&#39;ll humor you once. You mention knowledge and are somewhat spastic in your presentation of its definition. Answer me this: per your definition of knowledge, how much importance do you afford the ability to correctly spell? <BR> <BR>Steve_huff, you wrote, <i>&#34;I believe this is a man concerned about seeming literate, creative, intellectual, but he does not understand what truly demonstrates these qualities. Is not a hallmark of many sociopathic personalities an overriding concern with facade as opposed to substance?&#34;</i> Yes. Additionally, BTK may have earned a PhD but when looking over the snippets of his early communications, I see one who is quite concerned about how he is perceived.  <BR><!--/Text--></td></tr>
